Origin: applejack
Date: 2026-11-08
Reason: GetBestRoute2 asks the kernel for the route to a destination by
 connecting a UDP socket to it and reading the source address back. The
 caller's address usually has port 0, and macOS refuses connect() to port 0
 with EADDRNOTAVAIL, so on macOS the kernel's answer was never used: every
 call logged `GetBestRoute2 Resolving destination address failed` and fell
 back to a longest-prefix scan of the route table, which keeps the first of
 equal routes and ignores the routing policy a VPN installs. GetBestInterface,
 GetBestInterfaceEx and GetBestRoute2 callers (the Steam client among them)
 took that path. The probe now uses port 9 when the caller gave none; the
 port does not change the route. Measured 2026-11-08 with
 crates/applejack-engine/probes/netprobe under WINEDEBUG=warn+iphlpapi:
 two warnings and the fallback before, none after, the same interface (en0)
 on this host. See build/wine/patches/README.md.
Drop-when: upstream wine's GetBestRoute2 sets a port before its connect()
 probe; check each Wine bump.

--- a/dlls/iphlpapi/iphlpapi_main.c
+++ b/dlls/iphlpapi/iphlpapi_main.c
@@ -4855,6 +4855,10 @@
             if (v6) dst_addr.Ipv6.sin6_addr    = ipv6_default_addr;
             else dst_addr.Ipv4.sin_addr.s_addr = 0x01010101;
         }
+        /* macOS refuses connect() to port 0 with EADDRNOTAVAIL; the port does
+         * not change the route the kernel picks, and sin6_port shares the
+         * offset of sin_port. */
+        if (!dst_addr.Ipv4.sin_port) dst_addr.Ipv4.sin_port = htons( 9 );
         if (connect( s, (struct sockaddr *)&dst_addr, sizeof(dst_addr) ) == -1)
         {
             WARN( "Resolving destination address failed.\n" );
